From 6f1a381819e1ecaff118688e90ae2ee8b27acd71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessio Garzi <agarzi@sipwise.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 09:03:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] select the demo with the joystick

Joystick in port 2, a CD32 pad too (red button = fire), so the CD can
be used on a CD32 without a keyboard. On the menu page up/down move a
bar over the demo list, fire starts the selected demo (same code as
F1..F9) and right goes on to the credits like SPACE. On the other
pages fire or right go on to the next page, also while the page is
still being typed, as SPACE does. While the menu is typed the joystick
is ignored, so an early fire does not skip it. Up/down repeat while
held. The keyboard works as before.

The bar is the 5th bitplane flipped under the selected row, inside the
frame: the canvas shows through it in colours 16-23, which were unused
and now hold the canvas palette at half brightness.

Tested in FS-UAE on CD32 (KS 40.60, CDTV.TM ISO) and A500 KS 1.3.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dec/6.s | 146 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 143 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

